From: tabS3 bring-up <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add a driver for the Samsung S5K5E3YX sensor

The S5K5E3YX is a 5 megapixel CMOS sensor with an SMIA-style register
map (16-bit addresses, 8-bit data) that streams 10-bit raw Bayer over
two MIPI CSI-2 lanes. It is the front camera of the Samsung Galaxy Tab
S3 (SM-T825), on CCI master 1 of the MSM8996.

The driver follows imx258: the V4L2 CCI helpers, runtime PM over the
three supplies (vana 2.8 V, vdig 1.2 V, vio 1.8 V), the reset GPIO and
the 24 MHz clock. Two modes, 2576x1932 at 30 fps and 640x480 (4x4
binned) at 120 fps, both at 896 Mbps per lane; exposure, analogue and
digital gain, vertical blanking, flips and the test pattern are
controls. The register tables come from the module's vendor
configuration, as the sensor has no public datasheet.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig	2026-10-14 19:55:37.594882850 +0300
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig	2026-10-14 19:55:37.595760774 +0300
@@ -733,6 +733,16 @@
 	  This is a V4L2 sensor driver for Samsung S5C73M3
 	  8 Mpixel camera.
 
+config VIDEO_S5K5E3
+	tristate "Samsung S5K5E3 sensor support"
+	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+	help
+	  This is a Video4Linux2 sensor driver for the Samsung
+	  S5K5E3YX 5 megapixel camera sensor.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called s5k5e3.
+
 config VIDEO_S5K5BAF
 	tristate "Samsung S5K5BAF sensor support"
 	help
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile b/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile	2026-10-14 19:55:37.594929028 +0300
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile	2026-10-14 19:55:37.595799007 +0300
@@ -125,6 +125,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_RJ54N1) += rj54n1cb0c.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_S5C73M3) += s5c73m3/
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_S5K5BAF) += s5k5baf.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_S5K5E3) += s5k5e3.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_S5K6A3) += s5k6a3.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_SAA6588) += saa6588.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_SAA6752HS) += saa6752hs.o
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e3.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e3.c
